      "message": "refactor(motion): machining3d, multiaxis and quality read stock through Stock/Columns\n\ncamcraft-motion no longer names Dexel outside tests (M7.3 4/6). The\nre-machining masks are Option<&Columns>; the app wraps its prior grid\nwith Columns::of_grid (borrowed, no clone). Motion's own sims hold a\nStock on the column arm and read through Columns (above, top_over,\ntop_at) and Stock::measure.\n\nThe seam gains the edits motion needs (stock_sim::backend_edit):\nStock::subtract_flat, Stock::cut_chord and Stock::set_tops, each the\nold Dexel call on the column arm; the field arm cuts the flat tool with\nthe spanning flank and refuses set_tops by name. Columns::to_stock\ngives the rest pass its owned copy of the mask. quality::measure and\nrest_area return Result, as a seam cut can refuse.\n\nBehaviour-neutral: golden_cl, the finish3d/rough/quality goldens and\nstock_engine_agreement are byte-identical. Pinned by\nstock_seam::motion_names_no_dexel_outside_tests (source scan) and a\nbit-for-bit check of engagement_on against the direct Dexel read.\n\nFixes #587\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
